WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.802
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 1, Networking concepts, which is 23 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.802 --> 00:00:10.464
This lesson covers objective 1 point 8.

00:00:10.464 --> 00:00:14.628
Summarize evolving use cases for modern network environments.

00:00:14.628 --> 00:00:18.450
Today's concept: SSE versus SASE, and the job of a VTEP.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.840
Security service edge, or SSE, is a bundle of cloud-delivered security services.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:34.280
It combines a secure web gateway, a cloud access security broker, zero trust network access, and firewall as a service.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:40.150
Add SD-WAN to that security bundle and you have secure access service edge, or SASE.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:47.800
One part worth remembering: the cloud access security broker controls software as a service use and finds shadow IT.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:55.120
A VXLAN tunnel endpoint, or VTEP, sits at each end of a VXLAN tunnel.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.180
Its job is to add the VXLAN encapsulation as frames go into the tunnel, and remove it as they come out.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.461
For the exam, SSE is the security bundle, and SASE is SSE plus SD-WAN.

00:01:10.461 --> 00:01:15.120
A VTEP is the edge device that adds and removes the VXLAN wrapper.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.450
That's objective one point eight.
